actly matching the right endpoint slot is copied to the right\n  31:       two columns of the right active span.\n  32:     - A source run connecting the endpoint slots is stretched across the entire\n  33:       right active span.\n  34: \n  35:     Key insight:\n  36:     The left panel is a compressed legend for the right panel: endpoint markers\n  37:     stay two pixels wide, while connectors between endpoints expand to fill the\n  38:     distance between them.\n  39:     \"\"\"\n  40:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n  41:     assert g.ndim == 2, \"expected a 2D grid\"\n  42:     H, W = g.shape\n  43:     assert H >= 3 and W >= 7, \"grid too small for framed two-panel structure\"\n  44: \n  45:     frame = int(g[0, 0])\n  46:     assert np.all(g[0, :] == frame) and np.all(g[-1, :] == frame), \"bad horizontal frame\"\n  47:     assert np.all(g[:, 0] == frame) and np.all(g[:, -1] == frame), \"bad vertical frame\"\n  48: \n  49:     divider = _single_divider_column(g, frame)\n  50:     assert divider >= 5 and W - divider >= 6, \"panels must contain margins and active slots\"\n  51: \n  52:     left_panel = g[1 : H - 1, 1:divider]\n  53:     left_bg = get_bg(left_panel)\n  54:     assert np.all(left_panel[:, 0] == left_bg), \"left panel must have a left margin\"\n  55:     assert np.all(left_panel[:, -1] == left_bg), \"left panel must have a right margin\"\n  56: \n  57:     mini_start = 2\n  58:     mini_end = divider - 2\n  59:     assert mini_end - mini_start + 1 >= 4, \"left active region must contain two endpoint slots\"\n  60:     left_slot = (mini_start, mini_start + 1)\n  61:     right_slot = (mini_end - 1, mini_end)\n  62: \n  63:     target_start = divider + 2\n  64:     target_end = W - 3\n  65:     assert target_end - target_start + 1 >= 4, \"right active region must contain endpoint slots\"\n  66:     right_bg = int(g[1, divider + 1])\n  67:     right_panel = g[1 : H - 1, divider + 1 : W - 1]\n  68:     assert np.all(right_panel == right_bg), \"right panel must be blank before expansion\"\n  69: \n  70:     out = g.copy()\n  71:     painted_any = False\n  72:     for r in range(1, H - 1):\n  73:         c = mini_start\n  74:         while c <= mini_end:\n  75:             color = int(g[r, c])\n  76:             if color == left_bg:\n  77:                 c += 1\n  78:                 continue\n  79: \n  80:             c0 = c\n  81:             while c <= mini_end and int(g[r, c]) == color:\n  82:                 c += 1\n  83:             c1 = c - 1\n  84: \n  85:             in_left_slot = (c0, c1) == left_slot\n  86:             in_right_slot = (c0, c1) == right_slot\n  87:             if in_left_slot:\n  88:                 d0, d1 = target_start, target_start + 1\n  89:             elif in_right_slot:\n  90:                 d0, d1 = target_end - 1, target_end\n  91:             else:\n  92:                 assert c0 == left_slot[0] and c1 >= right_slot[0], \"run must connect endpoint slots\"\n  93:                 d0, d1 = target_start, target_end\n  94: \n  95:             assert np.all(out[r, d0 : d1 + 1] == right_bg), \"expanded runs must not collide\"\n  96:             out[r, d0 : d1 + 1] = color\n  97:             painted_any = True\n  98: \n  99:     assert painted_any, \"expected at least one colored source run\"\n 100:     return out\n----------------------------------------\ngenerate_input lines 285-290\n 285: def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n 286:     for _ in range(GENERATION_RETRIES):\n 287:         grid = _gen_attempt()\n 288:         if grid is not None:\n 289:             return grid\n 290:     raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid 9841fdad input\")\n\n================================================================================\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\n----------------------------------------\nmain lines 41-128\n  41: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n  42:     \"\"\"\n  43:     Fill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border